    "article": "**American League All-Stars Shut Out NL All-Stars 4-0**\n\nThe American League All-Stars dominated the National League All-Stars 4-0, with a stellar team effort on the mound. Justin Wrobleski led the charge, striking out five in two innings of work while allowing just one earned run. At the plate, Miguel Vargas made his presence known, hitting a solo home run on a fly ball to left field, his first of the game.\n\nVargas' power surge was one of the few bright spots for the NL All-Stars, who were otherwise unable to mount a threat against the AL's pitching staff. Dylan Cease earned the win for the American League, while Cristopher S\u00e1nchez took the loss for the National League.",
